INT. PAWNSHOP - CLOSING TIME

Glass cases of watches and wedding rings. A neon "WE BUY GOLD" buzzes in the window. A wall phone hangs near the register.

VIVIAN (60s, cardigan, reading glasses on her head) counts bills at the counter. The phone rings. She snatches it.

VIVIAN
Hello?

LEONARD (V.O.)
(over phone)
Viv. It's me.

VIVIAN
Leonard. Where are you?

LEONARD (V.O.)
Out front. Come to the door.

VIVIAN
I'm closing.

LEONARD (V.O.)
Please.

She slams the phone down. The bell over the door jingles. JUDE (20s, gaunt, duffel bag, hoodie) steps in, shivering.

JUDE
Mom.

VIVIAN
Jude.

She doesn't move. He drops the bag.

JUDE
I need a place to stay.

VIVIAN
You told me you didn't.

JUDE
I know what I said.

The phone rings again. Both of them look at it.

LEONARD (V.O.)
(muffled, from the receiver on the hook)
Viv? Are you there?

VIVIAN
Not now, Leonard.

JUDE
Is that Dad?

VIVIAN
He's been calling for a week.

JUDE
Mom, I didn't come here to fight.

VIVIAN
I didn't ask you to.

JUDE
I'm just...

VIVIAN
You're just what?

JUDE
Cold.

She stares at him. Then she lifts the counter flap. Holds it open. He crosses to her. She wipes his face with her sleeve.

The phone keeps ringing. She lets it.
